      "created_at": "2022-04-18T09:59:07Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-04-18T09:59:07Z",
      "body": "@giuliaghisini Do you have sources for this? \r\n\r\n> according to the EU law on the management of the GDPR privacy and cookies, technical cookies must have a maximum expiration of 6 months.\r\n\r\nI haven heard about or learned of any generic 6 month rule for technical cookies and have been working on the technical and legal setup for an international company with many European and world wide sites, also in Italy. \r\n\r\nThere are a number of lesser known 'extensions' of the gdpr in some EU countries or existing national pre gdpr legislation that hasn't been cleaned up yet after implementing the new privacy laws per country.  One I learned of recently is that in Belgium you're not allowed to collect anonymous statistics aldo without using any cookies: you always have to ask permission.\r\n\r\nIt's great to have the expiry dates configurable, but the 6 monthts is not a European guideline AFAIK (Italian maybe?) and if there is one I would really like to know about its source.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
